mdns-vpn-bridge — Debian/amd64 static binary + systemd unit + sample config
===========================================================================

Contents
  mdns-vpn-bridge            static binary (no cgo, no runtime dependencies;
                             runs on glibc and musl systems)
  mdns-vpn-bridge.service    hardened systemd unit (DynamicUser, sandbox);
                             starts the relay with -config only
  config.json                sample JSON configuration with placeholders
  README                     this file
  LICENSE                    MIT

There is no installer script on purpose: nothing here runs automatically and no
system file is touched until you copy it yourself. The commands below are all
manual.

Manual install
  1. Install the binary:
       install -m 0755 mdns-vpn-bridge /usr/local/bin/mdns-vpn-bridge

  2. Install the configuration file (root:root mode 0644; it holds no secrets):
       install -d -m 0755 /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge
       install -m 0644 -o root -g root config.json \
         /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge/config.json

  3. Edit /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge/config.json and replace the placeholders
     REPLACE_WITH_LAN_IFACE and REPLACE_WITH_PEER_OVERLAY_IP with your LAN
     interface and the peer's overlay address. Every key and its default is
     documented in the included configuration.md.

  4. Validate the file before it goes live. This is offline: it opens no socket
     and does not check that the interface exists:
       mdns-vpn-bridge check -config /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge/config.json
     A non-zero exit means the file is invalid — fix it; nothing has changed.

  5. Install the configuration reference, then the unit and start it:
       install -d -m 0755 /usr/share/doc/mdns-vpn-bridge
       install -m 0644 configuration.md /usr/share/doc/mdns-vpn-bridge/configuration.md
       install -m 0644 mdns-vpn-bridge.service \
         /etc/systemd/system/mdns-vpn-bridge.service
       systemctl daemon-reload
       systemctl enable --now mdns-vpn-bridge.service

  6. Verify:
       mdns-vpn-bridge version
       mdns-vpn-bridge status

Changing the configuration
  There is NO hot reload. The file is read once at startup; edit, validate,
  save atomically and restart:
       # write the new content, then validate it before it is live:
       install -m 0644 -o root -g root config.json.new \
         /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge/config.json.tmp
       mdns-vpn-bridge check -config /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge/config.json.tmp
       # Only if validation succeeded, save atomically:
       mv /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge/config.json.tmp /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge/config.json
       systemctl restart mdns-vpn-bridge

Uninstall
  systemctl disable --now mdns-vpn-bridge.service
  rm -f /etc/systemd/system/mdns-vpn-bridge.service \
        /usr/local/bin/mdns-vpn-bridge
  rm -rf /etc/mdns-vpn-bridge

Notes
  - The relay needs no privileges: the mDNS port (5353), the unicast link port
    and the status port are all above 1024, and joining the multicast group
    needs no capability. The unit therefore runs as a transient unprivileged
    user with an empty capability set. That user can still read the config
    because it is mode 0644.
  - ExecStart takes only -config, so the file is the single source of truth. A
    CLI flag given on the command line would override the file value; the
    shipped unit passes none.
  - Run exactly one relay per site; two instances conflict on the local
    mDNS/link ports.
  - Peer address, the asymmetric filter and the firewall rule that is the real
    security boundary are described in the repository README and in
    docs/configuration.md.
